    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka stands, once again, at a crossroads between retribution and reflection. The death sentences may satisfy a collective demand for closure, but closure without introspection is fragile. If the nation confines responsibility to 12 young men while ignoring the ecosystem of hatred that incubated their actions, it will have learnt little.\n\nFor the youth of this country, the lesson is blunt. Those who urge them to burn, attack, or \u2018finish the job\u2019 will not be around when they find themselves in the dock. When the fury fades, it is the foot soldier, not the firebrand, who pays. Justice must not only be firm, but also comprehensive. It is only when Sri Lanka demonstrates that incitement, whether by street agitator or cabinet minister, carries equal consequence will the promise of the rule of law feel real rather than rhetorical. Until then, the tears outside the courthouse and the cheers within it will remain two sides of the same unresolved national story."
