    "md5": "dc66c527d0be3bba0411efb318d4d08f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1680,
    "chunk_text": "ZKTOR: A sovereign alternative enters Sri Lanka\u2019s digital space\n\nSri Lanka has entered the beta testing phase of ZKTOR, a privacy-centric social media platform developed by Softa Technologies Limited, as concerns mount over external control of the region\u2019s digital infrastructure.\n\nThe platform distinguishes itself through \u201cprivacy by design\u201d architecture, incorporating multi-layer encryption, geographically bounded data handling, and structural restrictions on media extraction. Unlike mainstream platforms governed by foreign entities, ZKTOR is built on zero-knowledge principles that prevent behavioural profiling and data commodification.\n\nChief architect Sunil Kumar Singh, drawing on two decades of experience in Finland, has embedded Nordic governance principles of restraint and transparency into a platform designed for South Asia\u2019s demographic diversity and digital landscape.\n\nSignificantly, ZKTOR operates debt-free, developed without venture capital or government grants\u2014an industry rarity that insulates it from external financial pressures shaping data practices elsewhere.\n\nFollowing mass testing in India and Nepal, with Bangladesh scheduled for future phases, ZKTOR\u2019s Sri Lanka beta represents what analysts describe as a consequential shift: digital spaces that are designed, governed, and owned with regional intention rather than simply inherited from foreign providers.\n\nMinistry of Brands to launch Sri Lanka\u2019s first off-price retail destination\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
