    "chunk_size_bytes": 1569,
    "chunk_text": "Lanka Hospitals makes history with third consecutive Gold at TAGS Awards\n\nLanka Hospitals PLC has secured the Gold Award in the Health Sector at the TAGS Awards 2025, marking its third consecutive win and a historic achievement coinciding with the 60th \u201cDiamond Chapter\u201d anniversary of the awards organised by the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka.\n\nThe awards, themed \u201cDiamond Chapter: The Grand Honour of Excellence,\u201d recognise excellence in Transparency, Accountability, Governance, and Sustainability. This year\u2019s evaluation integrated advanced AI-driven criteria to assess the quality and credibility of annual reports.\n\n\u201cThree years. Three Golds. One unwavering standard. This is the result of a collective commitment to leadership and transparency,\u201d said Group Managing Director Chaaminda Kumarasiri. \u201cExcellence is never accidental; it is structured, measured, and delivered.\u201d\n\nGroup Chief Financial Officer M. B. G Wickramasiri added that the win affirms the rigour applied to financial stewardship amid a complex economic environment.\n\nThe award was received at a ceremony held at Shangri-La, Colombo. Lanka Hospitals holds Joint Commission International accreditation and is the first medical institution in Sri Lanka to be reaccredited by JCI.\n\nMogo Studios unveils trailer of Sri Lanka\u2019s first animated feature for global release\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
