    "md5": "0453596525e794bba216ab7053ae5235",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1525,
    "chunk_text": "Audiences will also meet some of the most influential voices shaping the Sri Lankan food and cultural journey, chef Dharshana Munidasa from Ministry of Crab, Lahiru and Don from Smoke and Bitters, booker prize winning author Shehan Karunathilake, chef Karan Gokani of London Hoppers and broadcaster and author Nihal Aththanayake.\n\nDentsu Grant Media has brokered a landmark deal, recognised as one of the first of its kind in Sri Lanka, with National Geographic India and it\u2019s commercial partners, providing a Friday 8.00 p.m. prime time slot with a repeat on Sunday at 1.00 p.m., prime time, targeting a highly valued audience as it will be broadcast across Sri Lanka, India, Bangladesh, Bhutan, Nepal and the Maldives.\n\nDentsu Grant Vice President Communications, Planning and Strategy, Bakmee Perera said:\u00a0 \u201cDentsu Grant Media with a legacy spanning over 60 years, has a strong footprint in the local media/ advertising sphere and is proud to be associated with Sri Lanka\u2019s long term content partnership agreement with an international network. National Geographic India, a member of the Geostar network and Disney International, marks Dentsu Grants foray into international content affiliation and management.\u201d\n\nWidely regarded as the Sri Lankan hospitality brand, Cinnamon Hotels and resorts leads as the title sponsor, with Jayaflava showcasing four of its seventeen hotels and resorts, Cinnamon Grand Colombo, Cinnamon Wild Yala, Cinnamon Bentota Beach Signature Selection and Cinnamon Life at City of Dreams."
  },
