    "chunk_size_bytes": 1548,
    "chunk_text": "Glowing Skin \u2026\n\nOh, yes, that\u2019s what most of my readers are keen to have \u2013 Glowing Skin \u2013 and they all want me to continue to highlight homemade remedies for Glowing Skin. And I just can\u2019t disappoint my readers.\n\nMash 02 pieces of papaya, add 01 tablespoon of honey to it, and apply this mixture on clean, dry skin and allow it to rest for about 15 to 20 minutes, and then wash your face with water and pat dry with a clean towel.\n\nDe-skin 01 avocado and 01 kiwi fruit and squeeze out the pulp from both the fruits and mash them until you get a creamy paste. You can also add a few drops of honey in this face mask (optional). Apply this paste, let it remain for 30 minutes, and then rinse with lukewarm water, followed by applying your moisturiser\n\nMash a ripe banana and apply it on your face and let it remain for 15 minutes and then rinse it off with cold water. The banana mask will make your face glow and even the skin tone.\n\nMix 01 tablespoon of honey with tomato juice until you get a thick paste and then apply this mixture on the face and wash off after 15 minutes \u2026 for smooth and glowing skin.\n\nCrush 04-05 strawberries in a bowl and make a paste and then add one tablespoon of honey. Mix it and apply to the face and neck. Wait for 10 minutes and wash it off with cold water. This wonderful pack removes blemishes and dark spots.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
