    "chunk_size_bytes": 1798,
    "chunk_text": "President, US Envoy to Delhi discuss expanding economic ties\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake (right) with US Special Representative for South and Central Asia Sergio Gor\n\nMeeting held in New Delhi on sidelines of India\u2019s AI Impact Summit\n\nPresident Dissanayake to address Summit today and hold bilateral meeting with Modi\n\nUnited States Special Representative for South and Central Asia and Ambassador to India Sergio Gor yesterday met President Anura Kumara Dissanayake in New Delhi for talks centred on enhancing economic engagement between the United States and Sri Lanka.\n\nIn a post on X, the Ambassador said discussions focused on reinforcing commercial relations and promoting regional stability through closer cooperation. \u201cStrong partnerships deliver real results for our countries,\u201d he said, adding that the meeting explored avenues to further strengthen bilateral engagement.\n\nSri Lankan exports grew 5.6% to $ 17.2 billion in 2025 with the US accounting for 23% of the country\u2019s merchandise exports, recording a 3.06% increase to $ 2,999.15 million. India comes second with exports increasing by 17.21% in 2025 to $ 1,035.72 million.\n\nPresident Dissanayake is currently in India on an official visit and is attending India\u2019s AI Impact Summit in New Delhi.\n\nHe is scheduled to attend a series of meetings from 18 to 20 February in parallel with the summit including a special dinner reception hosted yesterday by Prime Minister Modi for heads of state visiting New Delhi for the summit.\n\nThe AI Impact 2026 Summit, focused on advancing the responsible use of artificial intelligence for the benefit of humankind, is being held at the Bharat Mandapam Convention Hall in New Delhi with the participation of heads of state and representatives from the global technology sector."
